### 2. Update JournalBulkUpload.jsx to pass back compilation control
Open **JournalBulkUpload.jsx**, navigate to your **autoSubmitBatch** method (around line 368), and simplify the payload execution path so it doesn't process intermediate client-side time pickers inside the wizard frame:
```javascript
   const autoSubmitBatch = async (reqId) => {
    setIsCreatingBatch(true);
    try {
      const payload = {
        requestId: reqId,
        commonBatchRemarks: `Bulk Upload - ${selectedDate.format("YYYY-MM-DD")}`,
        vid: selectedVoucher?.VID || selectedVoucher?.vid 
      };
      
      const response = await callApi("/JS/voucher/create-batch-from-cache", payload, "POST");
      
      if (response && (response.status === "SUCCESS" || response.batchId)) {
        // ✨ Trigger completion handler up into JournalPosting context
        if (onSuccessSubmit) {
          onSuccessSubmit(response.batchId);
        } else {
          setBatchCreated(true);
        }
      } else {
        throw new Error(response.message || "Failed.");
      }
    } catch (e) {
      let msg = e.message || "Unknown error";
      if (e.response && e.response.data && e.response.data.message) {
        msg = e.response.data.message;
      }
      showSnackBar("Failed to submit batch: " + msg, "error");
    } finally {
      setIsCreatingBatch(false);
    }
  };

```
### Why this approach is perfect:
Since you don't have a parent wrapper managing layout routing tabs, this approach keeps your state fully self-contained. The moment either compilation path (Manual grid or Excel upload worker thread) finishes execution safely, JournalPosting.jsx unmounts its current entry wizards internally and hot-swaps the layout with <JournalPostingStatus />. You won't need to tweak or adjust any additional navigation files!
